        "original_id": "60b43c8c-b2da-5c16-8bc0-a9943feaa248",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Songs: \"Fingerprint File\"\n- Albums: It's Only Rock 'n Roll\n- People: Mick Jagger, Mick Taylor, Michael Kevin Taylor\n- Bands: The Rolling Stones, John Mayall's Bluesbreakers\n- Products: MXR Phase 100\n- Topics: rhythm guitar, bass guitar, phasing, jazz/funk\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kevin Taylor was born on 17 January 1949 and is an English musician.\n- Mick Taylor was a member of John Mayall's Bluesbreakers from 1966 to 1969.\n- Mick Taylor was a member of the Rolling Stones from 1969 to 1974.\n- \"Fingerprint File\" is the closing track on the Rolling Stones' 1974 album It's Only Rock 'n Roll.\n- Mick Jagger played the rhythm guitar on \"Fingerprint File,\" and his guitar features heavy phasing from the MXR Phase 100 effects pedal.\n- Mick Taylor played the bass guitar on \"Fingerprint File,\" and his bass part is highly jazz/funk-oriented.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
